WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.634
Hi! The 6, 7, 8 and 9 times tables can be hard to remember, but we can use facts we already know to help. Let's learn some tricks.

2
00:00:11.784 --> 00:00:16.362
6 times 7 is 5 sevens plus 1 more seven.

3
00:00:16.512 --> 00:00:22.314
5 times 7 is 35. Add 7 more and we get 42.

4
00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:30.858
For the 8 times table, double the 4 times table: 4 times 6 is 24, and double 24 is 48.

5
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:38.226
And swapping the numbers doesn't change the answer, so 6 times 8 is also 48.

6
00:00:38.376 --> 00:00:43.722
For 9 times 6, work out 10 sixes, then take away one six.

7
00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:48.306
10 times 6 is 60, minus 6 is 54.

8
00:00:48.456 --> 00:00:54.258
Look at answers in the 9 times table: the digits of 54 add up to 9.

9
00:00:54.408 --> 00:01:05.010
18, 27, 36, 45 and so on. The digits always add up to 9, so we can use this to check.

10
00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:13.074
Watch out! 7 times 8 is easy to get wrong. Some pupils say 54. That's wrong!

11
00:01:13.224 --> 00:01:20.178
Remember 5, 6, 7, 8: 56 equals 7 times 8, the digits in order.

12
00:01:20.328 --> 00:01:27.810
If you're not sure, use 5 times 8 is 40, then add two more eights to get 56.

13
00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:35.874
Your turn! What is 7 times 7? Pause and think.

14
00:01:36.024 --> 00:01:44.274
5 times 7 is 35. Add two more sevens: 49. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:44.424 --> 00:01:52.410
Another one! What is 8 times 9? Pause and think.

16
00:01:52.560 --> 00:02:02.058
10 eights is 80, minus one eight is 72. And 7 plus 2 is 9. Did you get it right?

17
00:02:02.208 --> 00:02:10.338
Here's another! What is 9 times 9? Pause and think.

18
00:02:10.488 --> 00:02:17.082
10 nines is 90, minus 9 is 81. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:17.232 --> 00:02:25.314
Here's another! What is 6 times 6? Pause and think.

20
00:02:25.464 --> 00:02:33.378
5 sixes is 30. Add one more six: 36. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:33.528 --> 00:02:44.106
Last one! Each box has 8 pens. How many pens are in 7 boxes? Pause and think.

22
00:02:44.256 --> 00:02:52.002
7 groups of 8: 7 times 8 is 56 pens. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:52.152 --> 00:03:02.802
Remember: use the 5 or 10 times table to help with hard facts, and swapping the order gives the same answer. In the 9 times table, the digits add up to 9.

24
00:03:02.952 --> 00:03:09.138
Say one times table each day, and you'll know them by heart in no time!

